      "timestamp": "2026-10-01T20:20:10.000083Z",
      "text": "What if the name and address are from a news article?",
      "source": "USER",
      "reactions": []
    },
    {
      "message_id": "1790886056.000113",
      "author_id": "U020",
      "author_name": "Theo",
      "author_role": "TUTOR",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-01T20:20:56.000113Z",
      "text": "The article mentions a named business and its office address; we should not assume every address in a news report is public business contact data.",
      "source": "USER",
      "reactions": [
        {
          "name": "eyes",
          "users": [
            "U013"
          ],
          "count": 1,
          "reactor_roles": {
            "U013": "TUTOR"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "message_id": "1790886105.000226",
      "author_id": "U006",
      "author_name": "Priya",
      "author_role": "TEAM_LEAD",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-01T20:21:45.000226Z",
      "text": "For the reviewed article, the address belongs to a named business rather than a private residence. If it were an individual’s location, it would require separate PII review. A publicly listed company address and a personal residence raise different questions.",
      "source": "USER",
      "reactions": []
